KZ3 patch 1100 (SPU pass 73): the WWS LS range probes behind the per-function LS gates.

spu_ls_read_probe's bufferSetArray reads (raw lsa 0xDF0..0xEAF) and spu_ls_write_probe_pre's code-buffer writes
(0x1320), both in image 2's policy-mode context, the context every WWS job runs in, only print, up to 48 and 6
lines; the caps are reached in the first seconds of a run (54 lines in a K2 run), after which they do nothing. The
range tests stayed on every LS load and store of every lifted job (3 and 2 instructions per access; the LS
accessors were 13 % of the audio SPU thread in SPU pass 72).
- spu_ls_dbg_armed (the snapshot SPU_LS_LOCALS takes per lifted function, patch 1082) returns two gates: bit 0 for
  loads (SPU_LS_LOWREAD, a watchpoint, or the read probe below its cap), bit 1 for stores (a watchpoint,
  SPU_SMC_WATCH, or the code probe below its cap). A set bit sends that kind of access through the full accessor,
  which keeps every probe; with a clear bit the fast path runs without the range tests, whose probes would have
  done nothing. The caps are named (SPU_WWS_READ_CAP, SPU_WWS_CODE_CAP).
Same LS and register results; the probes print the same lines. No relift needed. Upstream candidate.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): upstream gates (#445 merged upstream) + 1100's cap macros.

